body:
Option C is pushed. The head is `ddb2986f41fc948cd974f576bb6cbe287bf0a9bd`. The PR stays a draft.

- An Outside Arc re-entry after a lift comes down in air outside the stock, or on floor that is already cut. "Already cut" means cut earlier in the program order, at that depth, by the whole tool disc. In all other cases the op refuses the entry by name. `entry_warn::outside_air_check` makes this decision.
- New pins (`air_entry` lib tests, 13 passed): `outside_reentry_onto_cut_floor_is_accepted`, `outside_reentry_onto_a_partly_cut_disc_is_refused`, `outside_reentry_onto_floor_cut_later_is_refused`, `outside_reentry_without_an_air_lead_is_refused`.
- The decision file has the section "Maintainer decision".
- **`app heavy: offset_pass_start` did not finish on this head.** Thus it is not known if the 3 fig8 tests pass with option C.

Remaining work on this head:
- `app heavy: offset_pass_start` and `app heavy: pocket_pass_start`;
- `pass_start_engagement` and `pocket_pass_start`;
- the quick gate with `--base origin/main`;
- clippy on all touched crates. Only `camcraft-motion` is clean.
